Connectivity: opt-in support for legacy (pre-4.14) kernels

Enabled only with ro.bpf.allow_legacy_kernel=true on a pre-4.14 kernel:
- NetBpfLoad: skip the minimum-kernel gates; load every object with the ELF
  loader (libbpf can't on 4.9) and skip objects the kernel still rejects;
  create LRU_HASH as HASH (<4.10) and LPM_TRIE as HASH (<4.11) since userspace
  only reads/writes them; skip the kernel-stats write if test.o is missing.
- netd BpfHandler: skip the U/V/25Q2 kernel gates and the cgroup stats attach
  when those 5.4+ programs aren't built (per-app data usage accounting is lost).
- ConnectivityService: only use the local_net_note_op / loopback_access
  ringbufs (5.8+) if they exist; opening a missing one aborts natively.

